1
00:00:04,150 --> 00:00:08,418
A part comes back from the field. It passed every test at wafer sort.

2
00:00:08,438 --> 00:00:09,162
So what went wrong?

3
00:00:10,026 --> 00:00:13,706
Very often, the answer is already hidden in the test data,

4
00:00:13,726 --> 00:00:14,651
if you know where to look.

5
00:00:16,614 --> 00:00:20,019
ECID Outlier Analyzer takes a single device ID,

6
00:00:20,039 --> 00:00:23,714
and examines it against the full population from every statistical

7
00:00:23,726 --> 00:00:24,077
angle.

8
00:00:24,938 --> 00:00:29,068
Load native STDF, Spotfire, or SBDF data,

9
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:32,626
enter the target ECID, and set the threshold for each engine.

10
00:00:33,478 --> 00:00:35,828
Every detection engine is then one click away.

11
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:40,315
Classical statistics, spatial neighbors,

12
00:00:40,335 --> 00:00:43,860
machine learning, and deep learning all run on the same target,

13
00:00:44,718 --> 00:00:46,780
so a latent defect has nowhere to hide.

14
00:00:48,774 --> 00:00:53,324
Start with standby current, IDDQ. The target die is well inside the

15
00:00:53,337 --> 00:00:56,324
specification limits, so a normal test passes it.

16
00:00:57,194 --> 00:01:01,012
But against the population, it sits seven point four sigma high,

17
00:01:01,032 --> 00:01:02,619
and the univariate check flags it.

18
00:01:03,466 --> 00:01:07,566
Regression goes further. Threshold voltage and drive current are tightly

19
00:01:07,578 --> 00:01:10,821
correlated. Each value alone looks normal,

20
00:01:10,841 --> 00:01:12,971
but together they break the relationship,

21
00:01:12,991 --> 00:01:14,791
and the die stands far off the line.

22
00:01:16,774 --> 00:01:20,562
Nearest-neighbor residual analysis predicts each value from the eight

23
00:01:20,574 --> 00:01:21,399
dies around it.

24
00:01:22,242 --> 00:01:26,160
Ring-oscillator frequency rises from the wafer center to the edge,

25
00:01:26,179 --> 00:01:29,192
so against the whole wafer, the target looks ordinary.

26
00:01:30,038 --> 00:01:33,718
Against its own neighbors, it runs eight megahertz fast:

27
00:01:33,738 --> 00:01:36,188
a five point seven sigma spatial outlier.

28
00:01:38,224 --> 00:01:42,362
For multivariate patterns, four machine-learning engines score every die

29
00:01:42,374 --> 00:01:43,037
on the wafer.

30
00:01:43,906 --> 00:01:47,562
PCA with Isolation Forest, spatial-aware ML,

31
00:01:47,581 --> 00:01:51,774
local outlier factor, and a TensorFlow autoencoder all agree:

32
00:01:51,794 --> 00:01:55,569
the target ranks number one, out of four hundred forty-one dies.

33
00:01:56,418 --> 00:01:59,298
Each report lists the top contributing tests,

34
00:01:59,318 --> 00:02:01,168
pointing straight to the root cause.

35
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:05,880
Automotive screening adds two more views.

36
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:10,518
MPAT measures the Mahalanobis distance across all tests at once,

37
00:02:10,538 --> 00:02:13,450
and the target lies far outside the correlation ellipse.

38
00:02:14,306 --> 00:02:17,073
It scores a D-squared above twelve hundred:

39
00:02:17,093 --> 00:02:20,218
a tier-two physics maverick, driven by IDDQ.

40
00:02:21,070 --> 00:02:24,737
GDBN flags good dies surrounded by failures,

41
00:02:24,758 --> 00:02:28,508
and every die on the wafer receives a composite automotive risk tier.

42
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:33,382
Interactive viewers complete the investigation:

43
00:02:33,402 --> 00:02:35,932
wafer maps that highlight the target die,

44
00:02:35,953 --> 00:02:38,003
with hover lookup on every point,

45
00:02:38,862 --> 00:02:41,967
and a test summary report with loss, Cpk,

46
00:02:41,987 --> 00:02:45,792
and distribution shape for every test, beside its CDF,

47
00:02:45,812 --> 00:02:47,450
wafer map, and run chart.

48
00:02:49,422 --> 00:02:53,498
When a whole list of returns arrives, batch mode runs every selected

49
00:02:53,510 --> 00:02:56,435
engine on each die, and writes a single summary.

50
00:02:57,278 --> 00:03:00,083
In seconds, it shows which dies were flagged,

51
00:03:00,103 --> 00:03:01,878
by how many engines, and why.

52
00:03:03,842 --> 00:03:07,134
Every engine is validated on mock wafers with known,

53
00:03:07,154 --> 00:03:11,317
planted anomalies, backed by an automated suite of eighty tests.

54
00:03:12,241 --> 00:03:14,946
Fixed random seeds keep results reproducible,

55
00:03:14,966 --> 00:03:17,904
and every run leaves a CSV report and a log.

56
00:03:19,895 --> 00:03:23,100
The result: faster answers for every return,

57
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:25,557
visibility beyond single-test limits,

58
00:03:26,406 --> 00:03:30,231
evidence you can share, and the scale to go from one die to an entire

59
00:03:30,244 --> 00:03:31,056
return list.

60
00:03:33,018 --> 00:03:35,823
ECID Outlier Analyzer. Find the outlier,

61
00:03:35,843 --> 00:03:37,106
and prove the root cause.

